    },
    "treatment": "Same prompt and native tools in all arms; additional provider tools are available but optional. No forced API inspection or workspace_validate calls.",
    "timing": "Fresh corpus copies and independent grading excluded. Provider-specific setup is charged once, plus agent wall time including MCP startup, query work and native validation. Teardown measured separately. No prepared package index is required for Typelatch; any indexing it performs during use is already inside agent time.",
    "selection": "Two real upstream pnpm maintenance cases selected before these agent sessions, including one explicitly isolated dependency upgrade. The initial date-fns template is retained as pre-session amendment evidence, and date-fns remains reserved for external replication. Identical prompts across all frozen arms; fixed task order ABBA and reversed provider order per task across repeats. With four arms each occupies every ordinal position once. No tasks, runs or candidates removed after results; each candidate decision is separate.",
    "failurePolicy": "Persist preparation before work and run before launch. Preserve every attempt. Failed or interrupted preparation cannot be retried; interrupted or incomplete launches remain visible. Resume only a completed prefix. No replacements.",
    "evidencePolicy": "Private raw JSONL retained. Only completed public actions, source changes, independent test results, usage and timestamp metadata are eligible for export. No reasoning or assistant message bodies.",
    "limits": [
      "One task tests a real installed-API migration and one tests source workflow in the same pnpm snapshot. This narrow sample does not establish general API or monorepo superiority.",
      "A two-task sample with two repeats is not universal superiority or a statistical confidence bound.",
      "The public upstream repairs may occur in model training data.",
      "No immutable served model snapshot or sampling seed is available.",
      "OS file caches and provider prompt caching may be warm; cached tokens remain included.",
      "Fixture and prompt boundaries are procedural; no OS isolation claim is made."
    ]
  }
